Built with [Hydrogen](https://github.com/ATK422/Hydrogen), synced into Studio with [Rojo](https://rojo.space).

## Setup

You need [Rokit](https://github.com/rojo-rbx/rokit) (it installs Rojo, pesde, Lune and the other tools at the versions in `rokit.toml`).

```bash
rokit install
pesde install
```

Then open the folder in VS Code and install the recommended extensions when it asks.

## Everyday commands

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `rojo serve` | Sync the project into Studio (open the Rojo plugin and click Connect) |
| `rojo build -o game.rbxl` | Build a place file |
| `pesde run test` | Run the tests in `test/` under Lune |
{{#if stylua}}
| `stylua src test` | Format the code |
{{/if}}
{{#if selene}}
| `selene src test` | Lint the code |
{{/if}}
| `pesde add <scope/name>` then `pesde install` | Add a package |

## Layout

```
src/
  server/                  -> ServerScriptService.Server
    Main.server.luau       boots the server app
    Systems/               every system here is started by Main.server.luau
{{#if examples}}
      Visits.luau          example: player hooks
      Greeter.luau         example: use(...) and a network listener
{{/if}}
{{#unless examples}}
      Game.luau            an empty system to start from
{{/unless}}
  client/                  -> StarterPlayer.StarterPlayerScripts.Client
    Main.client.luau       boots the client app
    Systems/
{{#if examples}}
      Greetings.luau       example: says hello, prints the reply
{{/if}}
{{#unless examples}}
      Interface.luau       an empty system to start from
{{/unless}}
{{#if examples}}
  shared/                  -> ReplicatedStorage.Shared
    Network/               network objects, registered by both Main scripts
      Greeting.luau        example: a client event and a server event
{{/if}}
{{#unless examples}}
  shared/                  -> ReplicatedStorage.Shared (create it when you need it)
{{/unless}}
test/
  run.luau                 `pesde run test`: runs every *.test.luau
  Roblox.luau              loads game code under Lune through the Rojo sourcemap
{{#if examples}}
  Greeter.test.luau        example tests with Hydrogen.loopback() and app:replace
{{/if}}
default.project.json       Rojo project: maps src/ into the DataModel
pesde.toml                 packages (Hydrogen) and the `test` script
rokit.toml                 pinned tool versions
{{#if agents}}
AGENTS.md                  notes for coding agents (CLAUDE.md points to it)
{{/if}}
```

Packages install to `roblox_packages/`, which Rojo maps to `ReplicatedStorage.roblox_packages`, so game code requires Hydrogen with `require(ReplicatedStorage.roblox_packages.hydrogen)`.

## Systems and the network

A system is a ModuleScript under `Systems/` that returns `Hydrogen.define(...)`. `use(OtherSystem)` declares a dependency, so `OtherSystem` starts first. Hooks: `init`, `start`, `playerAdded`, `playerRemoving` and `stop`, all optional.

Network objects live in shared modules under `src/shared/Network/`. Both Main scripts register the same folder with `app:addNetwork`, because the server and client must register the same names. Every payload is checked against its GreenTea schema (`Hydrogen.gt`).

The [Hydrogen README](https://github.com/ATK422/Hydrogen#readme) covers the whole API: middleware, rate limiting, batching, buffer encoding and testing.

## Tests

`pesde run test` runs every file ending in `.test.luau` under `test/`, with [frktest](https://github.com/itsfrank/frktest). Tests require game code through the DataModel, as game code does: `require(game:GetService("ServerScriptService").Server.Systems.Greeter)`. `test/Roblox.luau` builds that DataModel from the Rojo sourcemap (`rojo sourcemap`), so Rojo has to be installed.

- `Hydrogen.loopback()` stands in for the remotes: `net:join("Alice")` adds a fake player, and server and client systems talk in one VM.
- `app:replace(System, fake)` swaps a dependency for a fake while the app runs.
- Stop each app and close each loopback at the end of a test (`test.on_test_leave`).
{{#if ci}}

## CI

`.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs on every push to `main` and every pull request: it installs the tools from `rokit.toml`, installs packages from `pesde.lock`, builds the place, runs the tests{{#if lint}} and checks the code with the lint tools{{/if}}. Commit `pesde.lock` so CI installs the same versions you do.
{{/if}}
